course: dictionary
lesson: 9605
title: Which meaning fits? Striker in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Picture a striker standing next to the keeper all game waiting for a long ball: the linesman's flag goes up every time, because that is offside.» The keeper, the long ball and offside are all football words, so a striker here is a football player.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Maddie, the best striker, got a detention for fighting and missed the girls' football tournament» still makes sense if striker means a football player. If you swapped in "a worker on strike", the sentence would make no sense, so that meaning is wrong here.
explain: The dictionary gives three meanings: a football player who scores goals, a worker on strike, and a person or thing that hits something. Stories and sport use the first most. News and history use the second, when workers stand on picket lines. Maths problems may count a striker's goals, which is still the football meaning.
fact: A striker is a noun, and its plural is strikers.
fact: In football (soccer), a striker is a player whose main job is to score goals.
fact: A striker can also be a worker who is on strike, refusing to work to protest about pay or conditions.
fact: A striker can be a person or thing that hits something, like the hammer that hits a bell.
fact: Phrases to know: star striker, centre forward, top striker.
exercise: «Connor and Tyler, rival strikers for two schools, both get picked for the county under-11s.» In this sentence, what is a striker? | A worker who refuses to work over pay | *A football player whose main job is to score goals | A coach who picks the team | A thing that hits a bell
exercise: «Picture a striker standing next to the keeper all game waiting for a long ball.» What is the striker waiting to do? | Pay the keeper for the game | Stop the match with a whistle | Sell tickets to the fans | *Score a goal from the long ball
exercise: «Maddie, the best striker, got a detention for fighting and missed the girls' football tournament.» Which clue shows striker means a football player? | detention | fighting | *football tournament | missed
test: Which meaning fits this sentence? «The strikers stood on the picket line outside the factory, asking for better pay.» | *A worker who is on strike to protest about pay | A person or thing that hits a bell | A matchbox | A football player whose main job is to score goals
test: Which meaning fits this sentence? «The striker hit the hammer against the bell to call everyone to lunch.» | A football player who scores goals | *A person or thing that hits something | A worker who is on strike | A goalkeeper who stops the ball
exam: Which sentence uses striker in its football sense? | The strikers are waiting for a pay rise | The strikers went home when the factory closed its gates | The striker was made of wood and hung on a hook | *The star striker scored twice in the second half
